From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] thd_logafni: leave out AFNI_serverlog on Windows

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: AFNI_serverlog() calls fork() and
keeps running AFNI code (an HTTP request) in the child without exec. Windows
cannot duplicate a running process, and the layer deliberately does not
declare fork(). The function has no callers in the AFNI tree, so it and its
declaration in 3ddata.h are compiled out under _WIN32.

diff --git a/src/3ddata.h b/src/3ddata.h
index b5775ff..10956ac 100644
--- a/src/3ddata.h
+++ b/src/3ddata.h
@@ -5960,7 +5960,9 @@ extern void AFNI_sleep( int ) ;
 #define AFNI_log_string(ss) AFNI_logger(ss,0,NULL)
 extern long long AFNI_logfilesize(void) ;          /* 17 Oct 2007 */
 
+#ifndef _WIN32  /* afni-win: fork() does not exist on Windows */
 extern void AFNI_serverlog( char * ) ;             /* 24 Mar 2005 */
+#endif
 
 void THD_outlier_count( THD_3dim_dataset *, float, int **, int * ) ; /* 15 Aug 2001 */
 
diff --git a/src/thd_logafni.c b/src/thd_logafni.c
index e65a562..1c0c27f 100644
--- a/src/thd_logafni.c
+++ b/src/thd_logafni.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
     Web server logs.
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
+#ifndef _WIN32  /* afni-win: fork() does not exist on Windows */
 void AFNI_serverlog( char *str )
 {
    pid_t child_pid ;
@@ -70,3 +71,4 @@ void AFNI_serverlog( char *str )
 
    NI_sleep(1) ; NI_stream_closenow(ns) ; _exit(0) ;
 }
+#endif /* _WIN32 */
